note {
	Donald, 1st of Colonsay
}

body {
	from LACHLAN McNEILL BUIDHE (KIntyre magazine) , A. I. B. Stewart:
$blockquote{
Mary's husband was Donald McNeill of Crear, the founder of the family of
Colonsay. Her second son was the first McNeill of Ardnacross. Annabell, the fourth girl, married Rev.
John McLean, Prebendary of Roseharken in Ireland, and her sister, Isabell married David
Simson, Minister of Southend and Kilchoman in Islay, whose father of the same name had
been exiled in 1685. Margaret married a relative, Donald McNeil
}

}
